{
  "$schema": "./unified-integration/config/ui.api.schema.json",
  "version": 2,
  "_help": {
    "api_keys": "Credentials for AgentEnhancements MCP services and the adaptive preflight selector. Each reference is an array of keys, e.g. \"TAVILY_API_KEY\": [\"key-a\", \"key-b\"]. [] or blank strings mean not configured and hide dependent cloud tools, even when a host agent has an environment key. First-party adapters (search-mcp) rotate keys per request; external stdio servers receive the first key. Do not copy agent login/provider credentials here. Never commit this file.",
    "connections": "MCP service endpoints, client IDs and model names only. OPENAI_BASE_URL applies to embeddings/vision MCP, not the agent's model provider, and includes /v1.",
    "preflight": "Adaptive preflight: mode 0 (off, default) or 1 (custom selector model). Mode 1 needs an HTTPS endpoint, sdk openai|anthropic, a model and a key in api_keys[api_key_ref]. Custom fields are ignored on mode 0. The former host-native mode was removed (AE-003); mode 2 is invalid and falls back to mode 0.",
    "mcp": "Shared by any MCP-compatible agent. Built-in local tools start automatically; search-mcp appears when any_of its provider keys is set. External entries stay hidden until their required references and an installed command array are configured. Changes are watched by the MCP gateway."
  },
  "api_keys": {
    "BING_IMAGE_API_KEY": [],
    "ELEVENLABS_API_KEY": [],
    "EXA_API_KEY": [],
    "FIGMA_TOKEN": [],
    "FIRECRAWL_API_KEY": [],
